main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ empty-pack base initialized: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/16: an empty pack expansion produces an empty list.  An
empty function parameter pack written by parameter name in a base
member-initializer (`Base(t...)`) is not reduced to `Base()`; the dropped
parameter `t` survives unexpanded and fails to resolve, discarding the
initializer.  Flip to CORE once empty function-parameter-pack expansions are
reduced regardless of whether written by parameter name or pack type name.
